<GuideLayout
  title="Pellet Sauna Stove vs Electric Sauna Heater | P1 Guide"
  description="Compare pellet sauna stoves and electric sauna heaters by installation, heat feel, remote start, operating cost, and sauna experience."
  path="/pellet-sauna-stove-vs-electric"
  eyebrow="Sauna heater comparison"
  heading="Pellet Sauna Stove vs Electric Sauna Heater"
  lede="Electric heaters are convenient, but many require dedicated wiring and can miss the wood-fired feel sauna owners want. A pellet sauna stove is designed to combine the convenience of set-it-and-go heat with the character of wood fuel."
  crumb="Pellet vs Electric"
  image={{ src: '/images/p1/ld-angle-sunset.jpg', alt: 'The P1 stove at an angle on a cedar deck with the sun setting through autumn trees', width: 1800, height: 1200 }}
>
  <section>
    <h2>Quick comparison</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Factor</th>
          <th>Electric sauna heater</th>
          <th>P1 pellet sauna stove</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Electrical work</th>
          <td>Often requires high-voltage electrical installation.</td>
          <td>Plugs into a standard 110V outlet for controls and automation.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Heat character</th>
          <td>Clean and predictable, but not wood-fired.</td>
          <td>Wood pellet fuel delivers a more traditional fired sauna experience.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Remote start</th>
          <td>Available on some models.</td>
          <td>Built in for convenient pre-heating.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Fuel storage</th>
          <td>No fuel storage required.</td>
          <td>Wood pellets are compact, widely available, and easy to store.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>When a pellet sauna stove makes sense</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You want the feeling and ritual of wood-fired heat without managing split firewood.</li>
      <li>You want remote start and temperature control without giving up renewable wood fuel.</li>
      <li>You are building or upgrading a sauna where avoiding major electrical work matters.</li>
      <li>Your sauna room is in the P1 target range of 210 to 500 cubic feet.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Bottom line</h2>
    <p>If your priority is pure plug-in simplicity, electric is familiar. If you want a more traditional sauna experience with modern control, the P1 pellet sauna stove is built for that middle ground.</p>
  </section>
</GuideLayout>
